{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WjEh4JhLatSKkvh2afdLkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Gandalf (full deep-think advisor) â€” Crucible Planning Session Summary\n\nGrounded bullet claims, drawn directly from the two member documents (Master Plan v2 / Stage 1, and Implementation Plan / Stage 2 â†’ Foreman handoff).\n\n## What Gandalf is (the locked North Star)\n- Gandalf is a **deep-think advisor** over any artifact/effort that does three things: **(1) diagnose** what's going on / what matters / what's wrong, ranked by consequence and able to return \"this is sound\"; **(2) situate** the effort in best-in-class knowledge by commissioning researchPrime *where warranted*; **(3) anticipate** via Parable-of-the-Oranges foresight and propose *vetted* value-adding suggestions â€” elevating, not merely critiquing.\n- The North Star was **locked verbatim by the user on 2026-06-20** and is the anti-drift anchor; it decomposes into six inclusion-test criteria **NS1 UNDERSTAND, NS2 SITUATE, NS3 ANTICIPATE, NS4 VETTED FORWARD VALUE, NS5 ELEVATES, NS6 COMPOSES (not reimplements)**.\n- The substrate is **vetted and must not be re-derived**: the converged research dive plus the diagnose-core PROTOCOL v2. Stakes = HIGH (FULL triage), persona = Fable 5, and because it's a **single-family** substrate, `cross_model:false`.\n\n## The defining architectural decision (post Shark-Tank R1)\n- Shark-Tank R1 produced **2 gated blockers**; the resolution was to **decouple the build into three increments**, each with its own GREEN done-state, so Gandalf v1 ships **without** the external Phase-0 ledger or the heavy elevation oracle.\n- **Increment 1 = the committed shippable Gandalf v1** (serves NS1â€“NS4, NS6) on the existing trio `agent()` seam, with anti-laundering as an **honor-system checklist**.\n- **Increment 2 = machine-checked anti-laundering**, which unblocks only when an external **Phase-0 commission-id ledger** (owned outside this cycle) lands.\n- **Increment 3 = elevation-efficacy proof** (the NS5/SITUATE claim), staged behind a feasibility gate so one expensive arm can't block the skill.\n\n## PRINCIPLE-D â€” the load-bearing invariant\n- The deterministic **done-floor / Foreman gate is the canary/test suite only** (`node --test test/*.test.mjs`); **no LLM or cross-family judgment is ever in the gate**.\n- All LLM/cross-family judging and the elevation A/B are **ADVISORY and isolated** â€” recorded as artifacts, never gating.\n- A **meta-isolation test proves** (not merely asserts) isolation: with the LLM/judge endpoint made **unreachable**, the gate still exits 0 on a conformant fixture.\n- Every boundary canary has a **discriminating negative** (a planted violation that *must* fail), answering the dive's \"canaries verify shape, not truth\" concern: canaries own **shape + rung-consistency**, the advisory oracle owns **label truth**.\n\n## Boundary canaries (the machine-checkable NS6 boundary)\n- B1 (zero ideation â€” that's Jumper's), B3 (premortem â‰  Crucible's Oranges engine: no regret/counterfactual fields, cardinality-1), B5 (diagnose exclusive to the core), B6 (no silent degradation), B8 (honest synthesis / rung-consistent labels), B9 (anticipate = future-state condition + enabling assumption), **B-honesty** (named-defeater + refutation_provenance or auto-downgrade), **B-ceiling** (single-family â‡’ max PROMISING).\n- **B2â€²/B7â€²** (content-binding) are **stamped BLOCKED-this-cycle** in Increment 1 and a canary asserts they are non-gating; they flip to passing only with the ledger (Increment 2 / H3).\n- Honest caveat captured in the plan: **B3 is a necessary syntactic invariant, not a sufficient semantic boundary** â€” prose can do cross-path cost reasoning with a clean schema, so an *advisory* (isolated) LLM check flags that and routes to Crucible.\n\n## Stage-2 wave structure (autonomous Foreman path)\n- **Wave 1** schema + canary harness + frozen constants (`prereg-constants.json`); **Wave 2** diagnose seam (NS1); **Wave 3** SITUATE compose (NS2); **Wave 4** refutation discipline (NS4 honesty spine); **Wave 5** ANTICIPATE / Oranges premortem (NS3); **Wave 6** score/label/synthesis (NS4, NS6); **Wave 7** integration + meta-isolation + journaling = **Gandalf v1 SHIP (committed milestone)**; **Wave 8** elevation-oracle harness + power-calc *code* (deterministic).\n- **Terminal semantics:** Foreman's **autonomous project-DONE = Wave 8 GREEN**; the **committed shippable milestone is Wave 7**. Stage-2 restructured every `## Wave N` to be deterministically gateable.\n- The Stage-2 Shark R1 (1 gated BLOCKER + 1 gated MINOR) drove moving all human-feasibility / advisory-A/B / external-ledger steps **out of autonomous waves** into HALT-gated follow-ons, and split SITUATE into compose (W3) + refutation discipline (W4).\n\n## Pre-registration: split into frozen vs power-calc-set\n- **Frozen now (Wave 1):** refuter budget **R=3** (exceeding HALTs, never silent-drops); firing threshold = value-if-true â‰¥ HIGH OR severity â‰¥ major; commission depth = 1; per-run spawn cap = 5; a skill twice in the commission chain â‡’ HALT.\n- **Power-calc-SET later (H1, not asserted):** non-additivity margin **G** (â‰ˆ10pp proposed) and oracle floor **k** (â‰ˆ10 real-history fixtures proposed) are **jointly set by a paired-test power calc** using ICC-adjusted effective N; if min detectable effect at feasible k exceeds G, **raise k or widen G** rather than ship underpowered. Min calibration **ICC â‰¥ 0.7**.\n\n## HALT-gated follow-ons (not autonomous waves; human/external preconditions)\n- **H1** feasibility + calibration + commit (G,k); failure â†’ record **\"elevate efficacy UNPROVEN\"** and Gandalf v1 ships *without* the NS5 claim (not a whole-skill NO-SHIP).\n- **H2** the bias-robust per-pillar A/B (SITUATE vs an abstraction-equipped direct-researchPrime arm; ANTICIPATE vs diagnose-core + generic premortem) â†’ **advisory** verdict only.\n- *